# Consulted by BuildKit for `docker build -f deploy/signal/Dockerfile .`
# (BuildKit checks `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore` before falling back to
# the context root's `.dockerignore`). A plain `.dockerignore` placed next
# to the Dockerfile in this directory is NOT read for that build command,
# because the build context is the repo root, not deploy/signal/ -- verified
# empirically; see the Dockerfile's COPY block for the load-bearing guard.
#
# configs/ is listed below as defence in depth and to shrink the context
# sent to the daemon. It is NOT what actually keeps configs/ out of the
# image: the Dockerfile's COPY list only names autogroupchat/, setup.py,
# requirements.txt, and main.py, so configs/ never enters a layer even if
# this file is ignored entirely (e.g. under a legacy non-BuildKit builder,
# where it has no effect and COPY carries the guarantee alone -- the
# verified-safe state this image was built and checked under).

.git
docs
tests
assets
__pycache__
*.pyc
configs
